A||N||6||U Wanna Race||Sub In Back?||||1||
Z||000000||U Wanna Race||10-19-2001||01:51 AM||||I want to put 1 or 2 12" subs in my fiero.  The easiest place would be in the trunk.  The only problem with this is that there is the engine back there too as well as the firewall.  My question is if I put a sub or two in the back how will it sound in the passenger compartment.  Has anyone done that before.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-19-2001||03:02 AM||||You'll need to port it into the passenger compartment.  But the port would be too long to be tuned properly.  So I wouldn't bother.  Stuff it up front if you don't want to lose legroom.  Bunch of people have done it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||10-19-2001||11:34 AM||||I've seen a few installs in the front trunk area. I never heard them, but I it would be better then in the rear.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||10-19-2001||11:52 AM||||do some searching for some of fierosounds posts. he has 10's behind each seat that he did something like 6 years ago. i think he said he had about .88cf for each sub. if you choose carefully there are 12" subs that can be used with that much air now. have to be careful with depth and magnet size though. i'm considering it myself. probaly be better for weight distribution too (compared to rear trunk, don't know about front. maybe not as good). <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||U Wanna Race||10-19-2001||02:35 PM||||I have seen the sub in the front in place of the spare tire.  But I would really like to keep my spare tire cause sh#t always happens to me and my car.  And I dont want to decrease the leg room by putting a sub by the kick panels.  This is because I am 6' 4" and all my friends are 6' or around there.  Does someone know how excactly to put the subs behind the seats.  That sounds like the best place to put them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||10-19-2001||03:04 PM||||Fierosound has two holes cut into his firewall for the subs, and his amp is kept on top of the spare-tire in a specially designed box.  His install is very clean and sounds good.  I just put a sub in mine, and didn't want to put holes in the firewall, so I'm just gonna have a small box behind the passenger seat.  My sub is a 10" Pioneer IMPP (500W) which only needs .8cf.  The box it's in right now is big and takes up ALL the room behind the passenger seat, but that's just 'cause I haven't had time to get over to my friends house to cut the box down to size, when it's done it should be alright.  There is also a guy in the Edmonton club with 4 in his car, all behind the seats, but his seats are pushed up a bit, probably wouldn't be a good idea for a 6'4" driver.  However, even one behind the passenger seat makes plenty of sound (IMO) in the small cabin of a Fiero.  That's just my input though!  Best of luck!<P>Brandon<P>ps. I talked to the install guy at Future Shop when I bought my amp and he says they sound great in the front, but you do have to take out the spare tire, and I'm not up for that.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Areakon||10-19-2001||04:51 PM||||I have 2 12" subs in my rear trunk. The amp is sitting behind the passenger seat. It sounds good enough for my tastes. Plus I get to have my seats all the way back and I have my spare tire.||||reg||1
